From: cargo-extracted-bot <cargo-extracted-bot@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:59:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Drop what cannot exist outside Cargo
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`SourceId::load` builds a `Source`, and two `Edition` helpers take a
`ProcessBuilder`; each gets a `#[cfg(any())]`, which removes it from the
build like a deletion but touches only its header, so upstream edits inside
them merge through. The `cargo_util` import only they used is marked the
same way. Public: the `resolver` submodules, and `Artifact::parse` and
`Dependency::set_artifact`, which the manifest parser calls. One doc example
is pointed at this crate. `resolver-tests` depends on the crate under the
name `cargo`, so its files, written against `cargo::…`, are unchanged.
---
 crates/cargo-resolver/src/resolver/mod.rs        | 16 ++++++++--------
 .../cargo-resolver/src/workspace/dependency.rs   |  4 ++--
 crates/cargo-resolver/src/workspace/features.rs  |  3 +++
 crates/cargo-resolver/src/workspace/source_id.rs |  3 ++-
 crates/resolver-tests/Cargo.toml                 |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

